  "fetchedAt": "2026-11-09",
  "bodyEn": "<p>Icons must be considered to be glanceable and discernible on glasses displays.\nUse rounded icon styles with a heavier weight to prevent halation effects.</p>\n<aside class=\"source-note\"><strong>Note:</strong> If you don't need custom iconography, use Material Symbols Rounded.</aside>\n<p>\n\n\n</p><div class=\"source-layout\" data-source-layout=\"styles-icons-columns-01\" data-columns=\"2\" data-layout-kind=\"columns\"><div class=\"source-column\"><figure>\n<img alt=\"Design elements should be anchored to the bottom of the frame.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/original/33544b1a-glasses_style_icon_unfilled.png\">\n<figcaption><b>Use unfilled</b> icons to avoid halation, or \"light bleed\".</figcaption>\n</figure></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"source-column\"><figure>\n<img alt=\"Design elements should be anchored to the bottom of the frame.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/assets/original/33544b1a-glasses_style_icon_unfilled.png\">\n<figcaption><b>Use a heavier stroke weight and rounded icon variants</b>for greater readability and harmonize with system typography, avoid thin strokes.</figcaption>\n</figure></div></div>\n\n<p></p>\n<aside class=\"source-note\"><strong>Note:</strong> For icons, check out Material Symbols. Available on <a href=\"https://fonts.google.com/icons\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Google Fonts</a>.</aside>\n\n\n\n\n<a href=\"https://developer.android.com/design/ui/ai-glasses/guides/styles/surfaces\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">\nPrevious\n\n\n        Surfaces &amp; Depth\n      \n</a>\n\n\n<a href=\"https://developer.android.com/design/ui/ai-glasses/guides/components/buttons\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">\nNext\n\n        Buttons\n      \n\n</a>",
  "textEn": "Icons must be considered to be glanceable and discernible on glasses displays.\nUse rounded icon styles with a heavier weight to prevent halation effects.\nNote:\nIf you don't need custom iconography, use Material Symbols Rounded.\nUse unfilled\nicons to avoid halation, or \"light bleed\".\nUse a heavier stroke weight and rounded icon variants\nfor greater readability and harmonize with system typography, avoid thin strokes.\nNote:\nFor icons, check out Material Symbols. Available on\nGoogle Fonts\n.\nPrevious\nSurfaces & Depth\nNext\nButtons",
